@startuml
' Traceability:
' - resilient-application-mcp requirements: R1-R23, R29-R32
' - resilient-application-mcp design: local SOP, manifest audit, release gates
title Local-First Application Workflow

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #0F766E
  LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #0F172A
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #ECFEFF
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  BoxBorderColor #CBD5E1
  BoxBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
skinparam titleFontSize 18
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Candidate
box "Candidate laptop (private workspace)" #F8FAFC
participant "Local AI agent" as Agent
participant "Application SOP\n+ workspace audit" as SOP
database "Local files\nCV, evidence, voice, job, drafts" as Local
end box
participant "Public MCP\nkit + selected-text review" as MCP

Candidate -> Agent: Start or resume an application
Agent -> SOP: Strict boot and workspace health check
SOP -> Local: Read privacy-safe inventory and timing data
SOP -> MCP: Audit manifest + check kit version
MCP --> SOP: Current / update guidance only
SOP --> Agent: Readiness, drift, and next action
Agent --> Candidate: Explain what to provide and why

Candidate -> Local: Add CV (PDF, DOCX, or HTML), job, evidence, voice
Agent -> Local: Preserve source, extract locally, build evidence inventory
Agent --> Candidate: Ask for photo choice and cover-letter signature
Agent -> Local: Build editable HTML CV and cover-letter draft

group CV review gate (one loop)
  Candidate -> Agent: Review CV and confirm or accept stated risks
  Agent -> SOP: Record current CV review against artifact hash
end

group Cover-letter release gate (three distinct loops)
  Agent -> MCP: Send only chosen cover-letter text for review
  MCP --> Agent: Feedback and high-level risk result
  Agent -> Local: Revise locally and record loop 1, 2, 3
  SOP -> Local: Verify distinct current drafts before release receipt
end

SOP --> Candidate: HTML/PDF outputs, readiness report, and receipt

legend right
Private local files never leave the candidate workspace.
MCP receives a privacy-safe manifest or text deliberately selected for review.
The service returns guidance; it does not expose private checker rules.
endlegend

@enduml
